# capability | write path | read path
#
# A capability is present when BOTH halves run: something writes it, and
# something reads it. A write with no read is a field nobody consults; a read
# with no write always returns the default. `physis-check capabilities` checks
# each half against the rule-1 scan, so a capability deleted from the source
# stops passing here instead of surviving in prose.
#
# Comma-separated alternatives satisfy a half if any one of them is live.

append-only observation log   | append                | read, read_tail
filesystem observation        | watch_fs              | by_source, read_tail
process observation           | watch_proc            | by_source, read_tail
bi-temporal validity          | narrow_until          | is_valid_at
workspace interface           | Workspace::record, remember | history, find
token-budgeted packing        | pack_with             | PackStrategy, chunks
line-window ranking           | Bm25Index             | rank, score
hypothesis fitness            | evidence, with_weight | fitness, status
world states from log order   | mutual_knn            | components, structural_descriptor
